cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use iPHAsimulator, please cite it as below."
title: "iPHAsimulator"
abstract: >-
  iPHAsimulator is a notebook-driven Python toolkit for building, validating,
  parameterising, simulating, preprocessing and analysing polyhydroxyalkanoate
  (PHA) oligomer systems. It generates chemically defined PHA oligomers,
  prepares Amber/GAFF2, GROMACS and OpenMM simulation inputs, supports HPC
  execution, and provides trajectory analysis and enzyme-PHA contact workflows.
  Developed at King's College London within the EU EIC Pathfinder project
  SATISPHACTION.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MMLabCodes/iPHAsimulator"
url: "https://mmlabcodes.github.io/iPHAsimulator/"
license: MIT
keywords:
